      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MAJARO GIRL (10) backs up from last Saturday's G1 Vicbred Super Series 2F Final where she finished midfield. Won twice in a row here prior, coming from a similar barrier to this to claim a heat of that series two back. Tackles older rivals but she is a talent. NIGHT FLIGHT (5) has had eight weeks off but was going well prior to that let-up, placing in five of his last six starts. Led from this barrier and stuck on for second when last seen at Ballarat. Could break through. SHES SKY HIGH (1) was solid enough when midfield in a Vicbred heat last start and draws for a soft run. ASPEN BELLE (6) broke in a Vicbred heat last time but her best form would measure up here. THE PASO DOBLE (8) should enjoy a nice trail and has been consistent with a string of top-three results including a Ballarat win two back.",
